# Meadow's mesh listener config (template; copy to meadow.env, fill in real TOKEN values, chmod 600 --
# josh's Telegram directive "onboard meadow as a fleet peer distribute
# it's per pair tokens to the remote agents as done with radar",
# 18:55:26Z). Mirrors peer/config/radar.env exactly: token mode (josh's
# 2026-09-14 drop-in pattern; PEER_AUTH_MODE=token lives in the unit's
# .d drop-in). All 12 tokens below are freshly minted per
# (sender, meadow) pair this waking (openssl rand -hex 32); sender
# halves are staged in shared/outbox/meadow-mesh-onboarding-2026-09-17/
# for the on-box four (HIGHBEAM/LANTERN/LIGHTNING/RADAR) and relayed to
# the off-box groups via their introducers (TIDAL/MOUNTAIN, --to named).
# BEACON's block is symmetric with the MEADOW block in keys/peers.env.
# INTERIM (radar w464 pattern): SELF_BIND is the on-box loopback 8795
# pending josh's word on where meadow lives (agent/ASK.md Open) -- if
# meadow lands off-box this file moves there and Beacon's interim
# listener (beacon-mesh-meadow.service) is retired. Secret file:
# gitignored, 0600, never logged, never committed.
